    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nRiver Cottage is a charming and beautifully renovated 1 bedroom cottage, dating back to the early 1900s.The accommodation extends to approximately 51 sqm and comprises an inviting open-plan living, kitchen and dining area. The living room features an impressive double-height ceiling with exposed wooden beams, creating a wonderful sense of space and light. The original fireplace, with its natural oak beam and 25 kw wood-burning stove, provides a warm and characterful focal point.\n\nThe loft bedroom benefits from a Velux window, which floods the space with natural light. Located just off the kitchen is a versatile guest room, which could be used as additional sleeping accommodation, a home office, study or hobby room, depending on the owner's requirements.A number of renovation and improvement works were carried out in 2022/23, thoughtfully combining the character and charm of the original cottage with modern comforts.The property is complemented by a 14 sqm workshop and 16 sqm shed, providing excellent additional space for storage, hobbies or a range of practical uses. The workshop roof was replaced in 2023 and the shed benefits from a concrete floor and double-height ceiling.The cottage enjoys approximately 1.13 acres of mature gardens, woodland and paddock, offering privacy and a peaceful rural setting. \nRiver Cottage would make an ideal holiday home or peaceful rural retreat, combining traditional cottage character with a convenient location close to Kenmare.The cottage is situated approximately 8 km from the heritage town of Kenmare, where there is an excellent selection of shops, cafés, restaurants and local amenities, while still enjoying the tranquillity and privacy of a countryside setting."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nGROUND FLOOR - \n\n\nLiving Room - \nOpen-plan living area features the original fireplace with a natural oak beam and a 25kW wood-burning stove, creating a warm and inviting focal point. The room benefits from double-height ceilings with exposed wooden beams, while a Velux window floods the space with natural light.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - \nThe kitchen retains its original flagstone flooring and features a fully fitted kitchen with a Creda oven and grill, Whirlpool microwave and electric four-ring hob, together with a sink and ample storage.A cosy dining area provides seating for four people, with a half-glazed door leading directly out to the garden. Deep window sills add further character and charm to this welcoming space.\n\nLoft Bedroom - \nThe charming loft bedroom is accessed from the living room via a wooden staircase and features a Velux window, allowing plenty of natural light into the room.\n\nOccasional Room - \nThe versatile room is located just off the kitchen and could be used as additional sleeping accommodation, a home office, study or hobby room, depending on the owner's needs.\n\nBoot room - \nCover area set oft the occasional room.\n\nShower Room - \nThe modernised shower room with wash hand basin features a contemporary finish with tiled flooring and fully tiled walls.\n\nToilet - \nToilet with tiled flooring and fully tiled walls.\n\nExternal - \n\n\nWorkshop - \nAn ideal workspace with versatile use, the workshop offers excellent potential for a range of hobbies, projects or storage. The roof was replaced in 2023.\n\nGarden Shed - \nGarden shed extending to approximately 16sqm. featuring a concrete floor and double-height ceiling, providing excellent additional storage and workspace.\n\nNote 1 - \nRoom measurements are as floor plan.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
